<title>UK: Shield Diagnostics slides on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Shield Diagnostics slides on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in biomedical company Shield Diagnostics Plc slid on Monday as a bout of profit taking set in after recent strong gains, traders said.</p>
<p>Shares were down 60 pence to 577.5 pence by 1040 GMT as the FTSE-100 index slipped 28.4 points to 4242.3.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a bit of profit taking after a good run recently,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Shield Diagnostics reached record levels over 900 pence last month after a strong start to the year. -- London Newsroom +44171 542 7717</p>
</text>
